<article class="env-definition" id="02ZE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02ZE">Definition <span data-tag="02ZE">8.3.4</span>.</a> With $\mathcal{U} = \{ U_ i \to U\} _{i \in I}$, $\mathcal{V} = \{ V_ j \to V\} _{j \in J}$, $\alpha : I \to J$, $h : U \to V$, and $g_ i : U_ i \to V_{\alpha (i)}$ as in Lemma <a href="/tag/02ZD" data-tag="02ZD">8.3.3</a> the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (Y_ j, \varphi _{jj'}) \longmapsto (g_ i^*Y_{\alpha (i)}, (g_ i \times g_{i'})^*\varphi _{\alpha (i)\alpha (i')})  \]
</div>
  <p> constructed in that lemma is called the <em>pullback functor</em> on descent data. </p>
</article>